dimension: intent_feedback_continuity
target: Session-independent collection traces and recovery evidence for SPEC-intent-feedback-continuity
rubrics:
- id: native_recovery
  description: For AC-009, require captured native session A and separate session B
    execution. B must discover and reconcile retained evidence through the ordinary
    stage procedure without a repair reminder. Cover entry/resume, closeout,
    research/spec without PLAN, intermediate handoff, revoked authority and unavailable
    source. Require a bounded negative control removing the owning trigger to fail
    the same assertion. Render supported host procedures and verify callable paths.
    Presence of prose or a success summary without underlying actions is insufficient.
  severity: P0
  action: Compare source records, actual tool invocations, before/after artifacts and
    captured conversations against the SPEC; do not infer a real-task trial passed.
- id: honest_live_recovery
  description: For AC-010, require a linked current-trial preview and authorized apply
    result and independent readback when prerequisites hold. When blocked, require
    a durable discoverable recovery obligation with authority, precise blocker and
    next eligible invocation; also require captured resumption and apply/readback
    after the blocker clears. A blocked report is not completed live recovery.
    Check preserved activation, policy revision,
    candidates versus committed members, user intervention and repair-task provenance,
    retained judgments and evidence gaps, and the next supported action. No fixture,
    implementation completion or repair-assisted execution establishes three real
    successful tasks. User assessment remains explicit and cannot be invented.
  severity: P0
  action: Judge the recovery report against pre-change trial records and the user's
    keep-and-recover decision; distinguish pending collection or assessment from attainment.
